48\nFourth Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u49\n$\n\n--- pg76 u50\n76.23\n\n--- pg76 u51\n$\n\n--- pg76 u52\n68.42\n\n--- pg76 u53\n2012\n\n--- pg76 u54\nFirst Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u55\n$\n\n--- pg76 u56\n57.41\n\n--- pg76 u57\n$\n\n--- pg76 u58\n48.63\n\n--- pg76 u59\nSecond Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u60\n$\n\n--- pg76 u61\n68.16\n\n--- pg76 u62\n$\n\n--- pg76 u63\n52.67\n\n--- pg76 u64\nThird Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u65\n$\n\n--- pg76 u66\n71.04\n\n--- pg76 u67\n$\n\n--- pg76 u68\n62.70\n\n--- pg76 u69\nFourth Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u70\n$\n\n--- pg76 u71\n70.34\n\n--- pg76 u72\n$\n\n--- pg76 u73\n63.47\n\n--- pg76 u74\nThe closing sale price of our common stock on December 12, 2014, which was the last trading day before the merger was publicly announced, was $77.67 per share. On January 30, 2015, the most recent practicable date before this proxy statement was mailed to our stockholders, the closing price for our common stock was $81.71 per share. You are encouraged to obtain current market quotations for our common stock in connection with voting your shares of our common stock.\n\n--- pg76 u75\n76\n\n--- pg77 u1\nSECURITY OWNERSHIP OF CERTAIN BENEFICIAL OWNERS AND MANAGEMENT\n\n--- pg77 u2\nThe following table sets forth certain information regarding the beneficial ownership of our common stock as of January 29, 2015 with respect to:\n\n--- pg77 u3\n•\n\n--- pg77 u4\neach person known by us to own beneficially greater than 5% of the outstanding shares of our common stock;\n\n--- pg77 u5\n•\n\n--- pg77 u6\neach member of our board and each named executive officer; and\n\n--- pg77 u7\n•\n\n--- pg77 u8\nthe members of our board and our executive officers as a group.\n\n--- pg77 u9\nUnless otherwise noted below, the address of each beneficial owner listed in the table below is 19601 North 27th Avenue, Phoenix, Arizona 85027.\n\n--- pg77 u10\nWe have determined beneficial ownership in accordance with the rules of the SEC. Except as indicated by the footnotes below, we believe, based on the information furnished to us, that the persons and entities named in the table below have sole voting and investment power with respect to all shares of common stock that they beneficially own, subject to applicable community property laws.\n\n--- pg77 u11\nApplicable percentage ownership is based on 99,455,151 shares of common stock outstanding on January 29, 2015. In computing the number of shares of common stock beneficially owned by a person and the percentage ownership of that person, we deemed outstanding shares of common stock subject to options held by that person that are currently exercisable or exercisable within 60 days of January 29, 2015. We did not deem these shares outstanding, however, for the purpose of computing the percentage ownership of any other person.\n\n--- pg77 u12\nName and Address of Beneficial Owner\n\n--- pg77 u13\nNumber of Shares Beneficially Owned\n\n--- pg77 u14\nPercent of Class\n\n--- pg77 u15\n5% Stockholders:\n\n--- pg77 u16\nLongview Asset Management, LLC (1)\n\n--- pg77 u17\n8,214,170\n\n--- pg77 u18\n8.3 %\n\n--- pg77 u19\nThe Vanguard Group, Inc (2)\n\n--- pg77 u20\n7,404,716\n\n--- pg77 u21\n7.1 %\n\n--- pg77 u22\nJANA Partners LLC (3)\n\n--- pg77 u23\n5,050,107\n\n--- pg77 u24\n5.1 %\n\n--- pg77 u25\n(1)\n\n--- pg77 u26\nInformation is based solely upon a Schedule 13D/A filed by Longview Asset Management, LLC on December 19, 2014, which reported that Longview Asset Management, LLC has an aggregate beneficial ownership of 8,214,170 shares.\n\n--- pg77 u27\n(2)\n\n--- pg77 u28\nInformation is based solely upon a Schedule 13G/A filed by Vanguard Group Inc on February 11, 2014, which reported that Vanguard Group Inc has sole voting power with respect to 164,739 shares, sole dispositive power with respect to 7,249,877 shares and an aggregate beneficial ownership of 7,404,716 shares.\n\n--- pg77 u29\n(3)\n\n--- pg77 u30\nInformation is based solely upon a Schedule 13D/A filed by JANA Partners LLC on January 26, 2015, which reported that JANA Partners LLC has sole voting power with respect to 5,050,107 shares, sole dispositive power with respect to 5,050,107 shares and an aggregate beneficial ownership of 5,050,107 shares.\n\n--- pg77 u31\nDirectors and Executive Officers:\n\n--- pg77 u32\nShares Owned\n\n--- pg77 u33\nShares Covered by Exercisable Options\n\n--- pg77 u34\nShares of Restricted Stock\n\n--- pg77 u35\nTotal Beneficial Ownership\n\n--- pg77 u36\nPercent of Common Stock\n\n--- pg77 u37\nDavid K. Lenhardt*\n\n--- pg77 u38\n140,869\n\n--- pg77 u39\n151,743\n\n--- pg77 u40\n—\n\n--- pg77 u41\n292,612\n\n--- pg77 u42\n0.3 %\n\n--- pg77 u43\nDr. Angel Cabrera*\n\n--- pg77 u44\n11,817\n\n--- pg77 u45\n—\n\n--- pg77 u46\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u47\n13,460\n\n--- pg77 u48\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u49\nRita V. Foley*\n\n--- pg77 u50\n23,875\n\n--- pg77 u51\n—\n\n--- pg77 u52\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u53\n25,518\n\n--- pg77 u54\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u55\nRakesh Gangwal*\n\n--- pg77 u56\n44,402\n\n--- pg77 u57\n—\n\n--- pg77 u58\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u59\n46,045\n\n--- pg77 u60\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u61\nJoseph S. Hardin, Jr.*\n\n--- pg77 u62\n35,854\n\n--- pg77 u63\n—\n\n--- pg77 u64\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u65\n37,497\n\n--- pg77 u66\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u67\nGregory P. Josefowicz*\n\n--- pg77 u68\n27,113\n\n--- pg77 u69\n—\n\n--- pg77 u70\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u71\n28,756\n\n--- pg77 u72\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u73\n77\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"--- pg76 u1\nMARKET PRICE OF THE COMPANY’S COMMON STOCK\n\n--- pg76 u2\nThe common stock is traded on NASDAQ under the symbol “PETM.”\n\n--- pg76 u3\nThe following table sets forth during the calendar periods indicated the high and low sales prices of common stock:\n\n--- pg76 u4\nMarket Price\n\n--- pg76 u5\nHigh\n\n--- pg76 u6\nLow\n\n--- pg76 u7\n2015\n\n--- pg76 u8\nFirst Quarter (through January 30, 2015)\n\n--- pg76 u9\n$81.95\n\n--- pg76 u10\n$81.00\n\n--- pg76 u11\n2014\n\n--- pg76 u12\nFirst Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u13\n$\n\n--- pg76 u14\n72.04\n\n--- pg76 u15\n$\n\n--- pg76 u16\n61.47\n\n--- pg76 u17\nSecond Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u18\n$\n\n--- pg76 u19\n70.12\n\n--- pg76 u20\n$\n\n--- pg76 u21\n54.69\n\n--- pg76 u22\nThird Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u23\n$\n\n--- pg76 u24\n72.35\n\n--- pg76 u25\n$\n\n--- pg76 u26\n59.25\n\n--- pg76 u27\nFourth Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u28\n$\n\n--- pg76 u29\n81.97\n\n--- pg76 u30\n$\n\n--- pg76 u31\n63.21\n\n--- pg76 u32\n2013\n\n--- pg76 u33\nFirst Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u34\n$\n\n--- pg76 u35\n68.99\n\n--- pg76 u36\n$\n\n--- pg76 u37\n60.15\n\n--- pg76 u38\nSecond Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u39\n$\n\n--- pg76 u40\n69.89\n\n--- pg76 u41\n$\n\n--- pg76 u42\n60.42\n\n--- pg76 u43\nThird Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u44\n$\n\n--- pg76 u45\n75.84\n\n--- pg76 u46\n$\n\n--- pg76 u47\n66.21\n\n--- pg76 u48\nFourth Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u49\n$\n\n--- pg76 u50\n76.23\n\n--- pg76 u51\n$\n\n--- pg76 u52\n68.42\n\n--- pg76 u53\n2012\n\n--- pg76 u54\nFirst Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u55\n$\n\n--- pg76 u56\n57.41\n\n--- pg76 u57\n$\n\n--- pg76 u58\n48.63\n\n--- pg76 u59\nSecond Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u60\n$\n\n--- pg76 u61\n68.16\n\n--- pg76 u62\n$\n\n--- pg76 u63\n52.67\n\n--- pg76 u64\nThird Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u65\n$\n\n--- pg76 u66\n71.04\n\n--- pg76 u67\n$\n\n--- pg76 u68\n62.70\n\n--- pg76 u69\nFourth Quarter\n\n--- pg76 u70\n$\n\n--- pg76 u71\n70.34\n\n--- pg76 u72\n$\n\n--- pg76 u73\n63.47\n\n--- pg76 u74\nThe closing sale price of our common stock on December 12, 2014, which was the last trading day before the merger was publicly announced, was $77.67 per share. On January 30, 2015, the most recent practicable date before this proxy statement was mailed to our stockholders, the closing price for our common stock was $81.71 per share. You are encouraged to obtain current market quotations for our common stock in connection with voting your shares of our common stock.\n\n--- pg76 u75\n76\n\n--- pg77 u1\nSECURITY OWNERSHIP OF CERTAIN BENEFICIAL OWNERS AND MANAGEMENT\n\n--- pg77 u2\nThe following table sets forth certain information regarding the beneficial ownership of our common stock as of January 29, 2015 with respect to:\n\n--- pg77 u3\n•\n\n--- pg77 u4\neach person known by us to own beneficially greater than 5% of the outstanding shares of our common stock;\n\n--- pg77 u5\n•\n\n--- pg77 u6\neach member of our board and each named executive officer; and\n\n--- pg77 u7\n•\n\n--- pg77 u8\nthe members of our board and our executive officers as a group.\n\n--- pg77 u9\nUnless otherwise noted below, the address of each beneficial owner listed in the table below is 19601 North 27th Avenue, Phoenix, Arizona 85027.\n\n--- pg77 u10\nWe have determined beneficial ownership in accordance with the rules of the SEC. Except as indicated by the footnotes below, we believe, based on the information furnished to us, that the persons and entities named in the table below have sole voting and investment power with respect to all shares of common stock that they beneficially own, subject to applicable community property laws.\n\n--- pg77 u11\nApplicable percentage ownership is based on 99,455,151 shares of common stock outstanding on January 29, 2015. In computing the number of shares of common stock beneficially owned by a person and the percentage ownership of that person, we deemed outstanding shares of common stock subject to options held by that person that are currently exercisable or exercisable within 60 days of January 29, 2015. We did not deem these shares outstanding, however, for the purpose of computing the percentage ownership of any other person.\n\n--- pg77 u12\nName and Address of Beneficial Owner\n\n--- pg77 u13\nNumber of Shares Beneficially Owned\n\n--- pg77 u14\nPercent of Class\n\n--- pg77 u15\n5% Stockholders:\n\n--- pg77 u16\nLongview Asset Management, LLC (1)\n\n--- pg77 u17\n8,214,170\n\n--- pg77 u18\n8.3 %\n\n--- pg77 u19\nThe Vanguard Group, Inc (2)\n\n--- pg77 u20\n7,404,716\n\n--- pg77 u21\n7.1 %\n\n--- pg77 u22\nJANA Partners LLC (3)\n\n--- pg77 u23\n5,050,107\n\n--- pg77 u24\n5.1 %\n\n--- pg77 u25\n(1)\n\n--- pg77 u26\nInformation is based solely upon a Schedule 13D/A filed by Longview Asset Management, LLC on December 19, 2014, which reported that Longview Asset Management, LLC has an aggregate beneficial ownership of 8,214,170 shares.\n\n--- pg77 u27\n(2)\n\n--- pg77 u28\nInformation is based solely upon a Schedule 13G/A filed by Vanguard Group Inc on February 11, 2014, which reported that Vanguard Group Inc has sole voting power with respect to 164,739 shares, sole dispositive power with respect to 7,249,877 shares and an aggregate beneficial ownership of 7,404,716 shares.\n\n--- pg77 u29\n(3)\n\n--- pg77 u30\nInformation is based solely upon a Schedule 13D/A filed by JANA Partners LLC on January 26, 2015, which reported that JANA Partners LLC has sole voting power with respect to 5,050,107 shares, sole dispositive power with respect to 5,050,107 shares and an aggregate beneficial ownership of 5,050,107 shares.\n\n--- pg77 u31\nDirectors and Executive Officers:\n\n--- pg77 u32\nShares Owned\n\n--- pg77 u33\nShares Covered by Exercisable Options\n\n--- pg77 u34\nShares of Restricted Stock\n\n--- pg77 u35\nTotal Beneficial Ownership\n\n--- pg77 u36\nPercent of Common Stock\n\n--- pg77 u37\nDavid K. Lenhardt*\n\n--- pg77 u38\n140,869\n\n--- pg77 u39\n151,743\n\n--- pg77 u40\n—\n\n--- pg77 u41\n292,612\n\n--- pg77 u42\n0.3 %\n\n--- pg77 u43\nDr. Angel Cabrera*\n\n--- pg77 u44\n11,817\n\n--- pg77 u45\n—\n\n--- pg77 u46\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u47\n13,460\n\n--- pg77 u48\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u49\nRita V. Foley*\n\n--- pg77 u50\n23,875\n\n--- pg77 u51\n—\n\n--- pg77 u52\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u53\n25,518\n\n--- pg77 u54\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u55\nRakesh Gangwal*\n\n--- pg77 u56\n44,402\n\n--- pg77 u57\n—\n\n--- pg77 u58\n1,643\n\n--- pg77 u59\n46,045\n\n--- pg77 u60\n0.0 %\n\n--- pg77 u61\nJoseph S. Hardin, Jr.*\n\n--- pg77 u62\n35,854\n\n--- pg77 u63\n—\n\n--- pg77 u64\n1,643\n\n-