'),\n dict(id='R040', when='12/10/2014', who='Bidder 3',\n   what='Did not submit', round=2, type='Financial',\n   terms='Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer in the final-bid solicitation after J.P. Morgan said its indication was unlikely to be competitive; out by the improved-bid stage (only the Buyer Group and Bidder 2 were asked to improve). Decided by: Both (target discouragement followed by non-submission). Exit reason: Value at or below market price. Count 1.',\n   reason='Stated non-submission; date established by the 12/10/2014 solicitation context (assigned to the due date under section 8.1 rule 2).',\n   quotes=[('P-025','J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive','Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer')],\n   src=['P-025','P-026'], review='Q5', count=1,\n   decided='Both', exit='Value at or below market price', obasis='Stated',\n   df=d(2014,12,10), dt=d(2014,12,10), wd=d(2014,12,10), basis='Inferred day', method='Assigned: deadline',\n   page=25, related='R039; R041', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R041', when='12/10/2014', who='PetSmart ad hoc committee (with J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton)',\n   what='Deadline revised', round=2,\n   terms='Deadline revised: after reviewing the 12/10/2014 bids, the ad hoc committee \\u2014 seeing the bids as close, noting positive developments since 12/03/2014 and viewing neither bid as the bidder\\u2019s best offer \\u2014 instructed J.P. Morgan to tell each bidder it must increase its bid and to submit improved bids on 12/12/2014; J.P. Morgan also contacted Longview on the evening of 12/11/2014 to confirm its continued rollover interest. Treatment: Extended. Due date (new): 12/12/2014.',\n   reason='Stated. Improvement request after the due date of a round already opened as final; an extension of that round under section 8.3, not a new round and not a fresh deadline set.',\n   quotes=[('P-026','the ad hoc committee instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid','submit improved bids on December 12, 2014'),\n           ('P-026','On the evening of December 11, 2014, representatives of J.P. Morgan contacted Longview','willing to participate in a potential transaction')],\n   src=['P-026'], review='Q2', count=None,\n   df=d(2014,12,10), dt=d(2014,12,10), wd=d(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   due=d(2014,12,12), treatment='Extended', page=25, related='R036; R042', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R042', when='12/12/2014', who='PetSmart (process deadline)',\n   what='Deadline', round=2,\n   terms='Deadline for improved bids. Both written bidders submitted on 12/12/2014; the board selected on the bids (approval 12/13/2014; signing 12/14/2014). Treatment: Enforced. Due date 12/12/2014.',\n   reason='Stated. The date passed with no further extension or late bids, and the target took its next step on the bids in hand.',\n   quotes=[('P-029','During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash','The Buyer Group initially submitted an oral offer of $82.50 per share, in cash')],\n   src=['P-029'], review='Q2', count=None,\n   df=d(2014,12,12), dt=d(2014,12,12), wd=d(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   due=d(2014,12,12), treatment='Enforced', page=26, related='R041; R047', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R043', when='12/12/2014 (with related events on 12/11 and 12/14/2014)', who='PetSmart ad hoc committee / Buyer Group / Longview',\n   what='Material process update', round=2,\n   terms='Longview rollover permitted and formed: the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group\\u2019s request to work more closely with Longview and to include a rollover of a portion of the Company shares managed by Longview in its bid (the Buyer Group said Longview participation might enhance its ability to achieve a higher price); Longview and the Buyer Group then entered a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information including bid price (not previously shared); Wachtell Lipton was instructed to provide a voting-agreement form to Longview. Bidder 2 had said accommodating a rollover would not affect its price and would be considered only after execution. The rollover was documented in the 12/14/2014 Parent\\u2013Longview rollover agreement (3,012,050 shares, $250 million worth, for Parent equity). Count blank.',\n   reason='Stated. One row for the rollover-support relationship\\u2019s permitted/formed step (section 4); the resolution would be at closing (not observed). Longview was not an independent bidder, so this is not a bidding-group change.',\n   quotes=[('P-027','the Buyer Group requested permission to work more closely with Longview','include a rollover of a portion of the Company shares managed by Longview in the Buyer Group\\u2019s bid'),\n           ('P-028','Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information','including bid price')],\n   src=['P-027','P-028','X-015'], review='Q1', count=None,\n   df=d(2014,12,12), dt=d(2014,12,12), wd=d(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   page=25, related='R005; R035; R048', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R044', when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Bidder 2',\n   what='Bid', round=2, type='Financial',\n   terms='Improved best and final offer: $81.50 per share in cash; J.P. Morgan confirmed by telephone the same evening that $81.50 was Bidder 2\\u2019s best and final offer. Revised merger agreement/transaction documents and financing commitment documents submitted. Count 0 (same unit as R038). Related: R038; best-and-final confirmation folded into this bid (same day).',\n   reason='Stated price; Formal (signal 1: bidder-returned revised agreement; also best-and-final response). Conditions Light: financing commitment documents submitted; no diligence condition stated.',\n   quotes=[('P-029','Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash','was its best and final offer'),\n           ('P-029','each bidder submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other transaction agreements','copies of their respective financing commitment documents')],\n   src=['P-029'], review='Q6', count=0, formality='Formal', cond='Light',\n   conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\n   df=d(2014,12,12), dt=d(2014,12,12), wd=d(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   plow=81.50, phigh=81.50, kind='Point', origin='Stated', currency='USD', allcash='Yes', cash=81.50,\n   page=26, related='R038; R049', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R045', when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Buyer Group (BC Partners-led consortium)',\n   what='Bid', round=2, type='Financial',\n   terms='Oral improved offer of $82.50 per share in cash; the Buyer Group stated it was working to increase the offer within the next few hours. Count 0. Related: R037; superseded the same evening by R046.',\n   reason='Stated price; Formal documentation carried forward (revised agreement submitted 12/10\\u201312/12 and substantially executable). Conditions Light (committed financing; no diligence condition stated).',\n   quotes=[('P-029','The Buyer Group initially submitted an oral offer of $82.50 per share, in cash','working to increase the offer within the next few hours')],\n   src=['P-029'], review='Q6', count=0, formality='Formal', cond='Light',\n   conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\n   df=d(2014,12,12), dt=d(2014,12,12), wd=d(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   plow=82.50, phigh=82.50, kind='Point', origin='Stated', currency='USD', allcash='Yes', cash=82.50,\n   page=26, related='R037; R046', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R046', when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Buyer Group (BC Partners-led consortium)',\n   what='Bid', round=2, type='Financial',\n   terms='Best and final offer: $83.00 per share in cash; revised merger agreement and other transaction documents and financing commitment documents submitted, in substantially executable form with few exceptions. Count 0. Related: R045 (same-evening improvement); agreed consideration on signing (R048).',\n   reason='Stated price; Formal (signal 1). Conditions Light. The board later noted $83.00 appeared to be the highest price the Buyer Group could offer, and that Longview\\u2019s participation (approximately $250 million of stock) was helpful in achieving it.',\n   quotes=[('P-029','the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash','in substantially executable form'),\n           ('X-008c','Longview\\u2019s willingness to participate in the Buyer Group with respect to $250 million of the common stock','helpful in achieving an $83.00 per share price')],\n   src=['P-029','X-008c'], review='Q6', count=0, formality='Formal', cond='Light',\n   conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\n   df=d(2014,12,12), dt=d(2014,12,12), wd=d(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   plow=83.00, phigh=83.00, kind='Point', origin='Stated', currency='USD', allcash='Yes', cash=83.00,\n   page=26, related='R037; R045; R048', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R047', when='12/13/2014', who='PetSmart board (with management, J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton)',\n   what='Target decision', round=2,\n   terms='Board reviewed the final bids, the process and the financing commitments; J.P. Morgan rendered its oral fairness opinion ($83.00 fair from a financial point of view), subsequently confirmed in writing; the board unanimously determined the merger with the Buyer Group advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders and recommended adoption \\u2014 subject to confirmation that remaining open points in the merger agreement were satisfactorily resolved, with reconvening if needed.',\n   reason='Stated. Preferred-bidder/approval decision; qualifications preserved.',\n   quotes=[('P-030','Following extensive discussion, the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement','in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders'),\n           ('P-030','the board\\u2019s determination was subject, however, to confirmation','had been satisfactorily resolved')],\n   src=['P-030'], review=None, count=None,\n   df=d(2014,12,13), dt=d(2014,12,13), wd=d(2014,12,13), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   page=26, related='R046; R048', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R048', when='12/14/2014', who='PetSmart / Argos Holdings Inc. and Argos Merger Sub Inc. (Buyer Group)',\n   what='Merger agreement signed', round=2,\n   terms='Agreed consideration: $83.00 per share in cash. Executed the merger agreement with Parent (Argos Holdings Inc., affiliates of funds advised by BC Partners) and Merger Sub; also executed the Longview voting agreement (7,424,591 shares to vote in favor) and related transaction agreements, including the Parent\\u2013Longview rollover agreement (3,012,050 shares). Signing is not a bid; numeric price cells and formality/conditionality cells left blank.',\n   reason='Stated. Agreed consideration recorded here, not as another bid.',\n   quotes=[('P-031','On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement','a press release announcing the transaction'),\n           ('X-015','Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares','in exchange for equity interests in Parent')],\n   src=['P-031','X-004','X-015'], review=None, count=None,\n   df=d(2014,12,14), dt=d(2014,12,14), wd=d(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   page=26, related='R043; R046; R047; R049', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R049', when='by 12/14/2014', who='Bidder 2',\n   what='Not selected at signing', round=2, type='Financial',\n   terms='Bidder 2\\u2019s best and final $81.50 was below the winning $83.00; the board noted neither other bidding group was willing to make a definitive offer above $81.50. Decided by: Target. Exit reason: Lower offer than rivals. Count 1.',\n   reason='Stated outcome (was still bidding when the target chose another). Timing assigned to the signing date (section 10.2).',\n   quotes=[('X-008a','neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50','lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group'),\n           ('X-008b','Bidder 2 had informed the Company\\u2019s representatives that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer','its best and final offer')],\n   src=['X-008a','X-008b','P-031'], review='Q5', count=1,\n   decided='Target', exit='Lower offer than rivals', obasis='Stated',\n   df=None, dt=d(2014,12,14), wd=d(2014,12,14), basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound',\n   page=27, related='R044; R048', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R050', when='12/14/2014', who='PetSmart, Inc. (issuer)',\n   what='Merger announced', round=2,\n   terms='Press release announcing the transaction (same day as signing).',\n   reason='Stated.',\n   quotes=[('P-031','issued a press release announcing the transaction','announcing the transaction')],\n   src=['P-031'], review=None, count=None,\n   df=d(2014,12,14), dt=d(2014,12,14), wd=d(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   page=26, related='R048', deal='PetSmart'),\n dict(id='R051', when='12/14/2014 (earliest supported service date)', who='Simpson Thacher & Bartlett LLP (adviser)',\n   what='Adviser service observed', round=2,\n   terms='Client: Parent / Merger Sub (Buyer Group). Role: legal counsel; earliest supported appearance is the executed merger agreement\\u2019s notice provisions; engagement date not disclosed.',\n   reason='Stated (service observed). No earlier date is disclosed; first mention cannot be treated as the engagement date.',\n   quotes=[('X-028','Simpson Thacher and Bartlett LLP','Attention: Ryerson Symons')],\n   src=['X-028'], review='Q5', count=None,\n   df=d(2014,12,14), dt=d(2014,12,14), wd=d(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n   page='A-46', related='', deal='PetSmart'),\n]\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- validation\nerrors = []\nids = [r['id'] for r in ROWS]\nif len(set(ids)) != len(ids): errors.append('duplicate row ids')\nprev = None\nfor r in ROWS:\n    if prev and r['wd'] < prev: errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: working date decreases vs previous\")\n    prev = r['wd']\n    if r.get('df') and r.get('dt') and not (r['df'] <= r['wd'] <= r['dt']): errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: wd outside bounds\")\n    if r.get('df') and not r.get('dt') and r['wd'] < r['df']: errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: wd before df\")\n    b = r['basis']; m = r['method']\n    if b == 'Reported day' and m != 'Reported': errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: basis/method mismatch {b}/{m}\")\n    if b == 'Inferred day' and m != 'Inferred': errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: basis/method mismatch {b}/{m}\")\n    if r.get('df') and r['df'] > r['dt']: errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: df>dt\")\n    try:\n        why = make_why(r['reason'], r['quotes'])\n    except Exception as e:\n        errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: {e}\")\n\n# verify all source ids exist\nfor r in ROWS:\n    for s in r['src']:\n        if s not in REG: errors.append(f\"{r['id']}: unknown source {s}\")\n\nif errors:\n    print('ERRORS:')\n    for e in errors: print(' -', e)\nelse:\n    print('All structural validations passed.')\n\n# write out for the workbook builder\njson.dump({'rows': [{k: (v.isoformat() if isinstance(v, dt.date) else v) for k, v in r.items()\n                     if k not in ('quotes',)} for r in ROWS]}, open('/tmp/opencode/rows.json','w'), indent=1)\nprint('rows written:', len(ROWS))\n"},"output":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/build_petsmart.py","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/build_petsmart.py"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/build_petsmart.py\", \"content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n# Build PetSmart deal ledger workbook (SEC_Deal_Ledger_Extraction_Instruction, rev 19 Sep 2026).\\nimport json, re, datetime as dt\\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\\n\\nCORPUS = [json.loads(l) for l in open('/tmp/opencode/corpus.jsonl')]\\nUNIT = {(r['pi'], r['ui']): r for r in CORPUS}\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- source registry\\nP_ITEMS = [\\n    ('P-001', 27, 6,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-002', 27, 7,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-003', 27, 8,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-004', 27, 9,  'Background of the Merger', True),\\n    ('P-005', 28, 1,  'Background of the Merger', True),\\n    ('P-006', 28, 2,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-007', 28, 3,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-008', 28, 4,  'Background of the Merger', True),\\n    ('P-009', 29, 1,  'Background of the Merger', True),\\n    ('P-010', 29, 2,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-011', 29, 3,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-012', 29, 4,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-013', 29, 5,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-014', 29, 6,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-015', 30, 1,  'Background of the Merger', True),\\n    ('P-016', 30, 2,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-017', 30, 3,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-018', 30, 4,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-019', 30, 5,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-020', 30, 6,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-021', 31, 1,  'Background of the Merger', True),\\n    ('P-022', 31, 2,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-023', 31, 3,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-024', 31, 4,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-025', 31, 5,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-026', 31, 6,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-027', 31, 7,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-028', 32, 1,  'Background of the Merger', True),\\n    ('P-029', 32, 2,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-030', 32, 3,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n    ('P-031', 32, 4,  'Background of the Merger', False),\\n]\\nX_ITEMS = [\\n    ('X-001', 7, 9,  'Summary — Definitions'),\\n    ('X-002', 8, 10, 'Summary — Effect of Merger'),\\n    ('X-003', 8, 12, 'Summary — Record Date and Quorum'),\\n    ('X-004', 9, 18, 'Summary — Voting Support Agreement'),\\n    ('X-005', 10, 14, 'Questions and Answers'),\\n    ('X-006', 11, 17, 'Questions and Answers'),\\n    ('X-007', 22, 5, 'The Parties to the Merger Agreement'),\\n    ('X-008', 33, 3, 'Reasons for the Merger'),\\n    ('X-009', 34, 13, 'Reasons for the Merger'),\\n    ('X-010', 34, 17, 'Reasons for the Merger'),\\n    ('X-011', 40, 3, 'Financing'),\\n    ('X-012', 40, 5, 'Financing — Debt'),\\n    ('X-013', 40, 7, 'Financing — Equity'),\\n    ('X-014', 40, 9, 'Financing'),\\n    ('X-015', 41, 2, 'Financing — Equity'),\\n    ('X-016', 41, 11, 'Financing — Equity'),\\n    ('X-017', 41, 13, 'Financing — Debt'),\\n    ('X-018', 58, 3, 'Regulatory Approvals'),\\n    ('X-019', 58, 6, 'Regulatory Approvals'),\\n    ('X-020', 58, 8, 'Litigation'),\\n    ('X-021', 82, 74, 'Market Price of the Company\\\\u2019s Common Stock'),\\n    ('X-022', 83, 26, 'Security Ownership of Certain Beneficial Owners and Management'),\\n    ('X-023', 26, 7, 'Solicitation of Proxies'),\\n    ('X-024', 2, 8, 'Proxy Statement — Date'),\\n    ('X-025', 23, 4, 'The Special Meeting'),\\n    ('X-026', 32, 8, 'Reasons for the Merger'),\\n    ('X-027', 34, 6, 'Reasons for the Merger — Likelihood of Completion'),\\n    ('X-028', 143, 7, 'The Merger Agreement — Notices (Annex A)'),\\n]\\n\\ndef split_unit_text(text, cut_points):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Split a long unit at cut-point snippets; returns list of parts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    norm = normalize(text)\\n    idxs = []\\n    for cp in cut_points:\\n        n = normalize(cp)\\n        i = norm.find(n)\\n        if i < 0:\\n            raise ValueError('cut point not found: ' + cp[:40])\\n        idxs.append(i)\\n    parts, prev = [], 0\\n    # convert normalized index back to original: normalized replaces same-length chars\\n    # our normalize is 1:1 per char (quote chars + dashes), so indices align\\n    for i in idxs:\\n        parts.append(text[prev:i].strip())\\n        prev = i\\n    parts.append(text[prev:].strip())\\n    return parts\\n\\ndef normalize(s):\\n    s = s.replace('\\\\u2019', \\\"'\\\").replace('\\\\u2018', \\\"'\\\")\\n    s = s.replace('\\\\u201c', '\\\"').replace('\\\\u201d', '\\\"')\\n    s = s.replace('\\\\u2013', '-').replace('\\\\u2014', '-')\\n    s = s.replace('\\\\u00a0', ' ')\\n    return s\\n\\nREG = OrderedDict()   # id -> dict(text, page, section, pi, ui)\\nfor pid, pi, ui, sec, cont in P_ITEMS:\\n    t = UNIT[(pi, ui)]['text']\\n    REG[pid] = {'text': t, 'page': UNIT[(pi, ui)]['page'], 'section': sec, 'pi': pi, 'ui': ui, 'cont': cont}\\nfor xid, pi, ui, sec in X_ITEMS:\\n    t = UNIT[(pi, ui)]['text']\\n    if xid == 'X-008':\\n        parts = split_unit_text(t, ['The board noted that Bidder 2', 'Among other things, the Buyer Group informed'])\\n        for i, ch in enumerate(['a', 'b', 'c']):\\n            REG[f'X-008{ch}'] = {'text': parts[i], 'page': '27', 'section': sec, 'pi': pi, 'ui': ui, 'cont': i > 0}\\n    else:\\n        REG[xid] = {'text': t, 'page': UNIT[(pi, ui)]['page'], 'section': sec, 'pi': pi, 'ui': ui, 'cont': False}\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- quote extraction\\ndef toks(s):\\n    out = []\\n    for m in re.finditer(r'\\\\S+', s):\\n        out.append((normalize(m.group(0)).lower(), m.start(), m.end()))\\n    return out\\n\\ndef find_quote(src_id, start, end):\\n    text = REG[src_id]['text']\\n    tt = toks(text)\\n    st = toks(start); et = toks(end)\\n    sn = [x[0] for x in st]; en = [x[0] for x in et]\\n    wn = [x[0] for x in tt]\\n    # find start token sequence\\n    si = None\\n    for i in range(len(wn) - len(sn) + 1):\\n        if wn[i:i+len(sn)] == sn:\\n            si = i; break\\n    if si is None:\\n        raise ValueError(f'[{src_id}] start not found: {start[:60]!r}')\\n    # find end token sequence at/after start\\n    ei = None\\n    for j in range(si + len(sn) - 1, len(wn) - len(en) + 1):\\n        if wn[j:j+len(en)] == en:\\n            ei = j + len(en) - 1; break\\n    if ei is None:\\n        raise ValueError(f'[{src_id}] end not found: {end[:60]!r}')\\n    return text[tt[si][1]:tt[ei][2]]\\n\\ndef make_why(reason, quotes):\\n    parts = [reason]\\n    for qid, s, e in quotes:\\n        q = find_quote(qid, s, e)\\n        parts.append(f'\\\\u201c{q}\\\\u201d (p.{REG[qid][\\\"page\\\"]}).')\\n    return ' '.join(parts)\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ledger rows\\nD = dt.date\\ndef d(y, m, dd): return D(y, m, dd)\\n\\nROWS = [\\n dict(id='R001', when='06/18/2014', who='PetSmart board (with management, a financial advisor and Wachtell Lipton)',\\n   what='Material process update', round=0,\\n   terms='Board reviewed strategic and financial alternatives; determined to explore capital-structure changes with a focus on returning capital to stockholders; established the ad hoc committee (Chairman Gregory Josefowicz, Rakesh Gangwal, Thomas Stemberg); authorized the vetting and retention of a financial advisor.',\\n   reason='Stated. First board step in the exploration that became the sale process; not itself a sale decision.',\\n   quotes=[('P-004', 'At a meeting on June 18, 2014', 'focus on returning capital to stockholders'),\\n           ('P-005', 'Chairman Gregory Josefowicz', 'to assist in the review')],\\n   src=['P-004','P-005'], review='Q1', count=None,\\n   df=d(2014,6,18), dt=d(2014,6,18), wd=d(2014,6,18), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n   page=21, related='', deal='PetSmart'),\\n dict(id