{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825298886,"sessionID":"ses_f4628fb5effez2Rp2Ib8TcXtcB","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e6965c001ic39x3NiX328r0_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f4628fb5effez2Rp2Ib8TcXtcB","messageID":"msg_0b9e6965c001ic39x3NiX328r0","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and verified. Here is the delivery.\n\n## Workbook\n\n**`/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx`** — four visible sheets, two hidden, 51 ledger rows:\n\n- **Deal ledger** — 51 rows (R001–R051), 14 visible columns plus 25 collapsed expandable fields (Row id, Count, date bounds, price, cash, Conditions detail, Due date/treatment, Round finality, outcome fields, Page, Related rows); filters, frozen headers, drop-downs on all controlled categories; every Source cell links to its main paragraph on the Source text sheet.\n- **Summary** — status/commercial account, deal facts, process and round map, participants and advisers, ledger-derived count formulas with filing assertions, stage balances, comparability inputs and glossary.\n- **Questions** — Q1–Q9 with recommended answers, affected rows, consequences, Status = Pending; section-13 check results beneath.\n- **Source text** — the complete Background of the Merger (P-001–P-031, pp. 21–26) plus every additional passage used (X-001–X-029), as filed text with pages.\n- Hidden **AI original** (values-only baseline of the Deal ledger) and **Lists** (exact drop-down values).\n\n## The deal in brief\n\nPetSmart — pressured by JANA (9.9%, July 3) and Longview (July 7) — decided on 08/13/2014 to explore a sale, announced it 08/19, and excluded antitrust-risky Industry Participant. J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 parties; 15 financial buyers signed NDAs/standstills in the first week of October; six submitted non-binding IOIs on 10/30 (Buyer Group $81–83; another $80–85; Bidder 2 $78→$81–84). On 11/03 the four bidders at/above $80 advanced to the final round; two combined as \"Bidder 3\" (4→3 units). Final bids 12/10: $80.70 (Buyer Group), $80.35 (Bidder 2), Bidder 3 uncompetitive (≤~$78). After the 12/10→12/12 extension, Bidder 2 confirmed $81.50 best-and-final and the Buyer Group moved $82.50→**$83.00 best and final**. Board approval 12/13; **signed and announced 12/14/2014** at $83.00 all cash (38.8% premium to the 07/02 unaffected price), with Longview rolling over 3,012,050 shares and voting 7,424,591 shares. Observed outcome: signed with the Buyer Group; no post-signing competing proposal as of 02/02/2015; closing not observed in the filing.\n\n## Most consequential review items (recommendations in Questions)\n\n1. **Q1 round map** — two rounds: R1 anchored on the October NDA wave (Not final), R2 final round 11/03 (Announced as final); rejected candidates (08/13 decision, 08/19 release, Industry Participant contacts, 10/30 deadline) and a rejected R3 boundary are each evidenced.\n2. **Q3 Bidder 3 membership** — the filing doesn't name the two members; recommended reading = the two final-round bidders besides the Buyer Group and Bidder 2, with Count-0 \"Inferred: identity\" closures.\n3. **Q4 counts** — six submitters (Background) vs \"5 bidder groups\" (Reasons): keep six and preserve the conflict; the nine non-submitters assume all six submitters were among the 15 signers.\n4. **Q5 inferred closings** — the 9-residual, plus the stated exits of Bidder 3 (Both; value at/below market) and Bidder 2 (Target; lower offer than rivals); Industry Participant never entered and has no outcome row.\n5. **Q2/Q6/Q7/Q8** — deadline treatments, formal/conditions levels (IOIs Informal/Insufficient evidence; final bids Formal/Light), the ≤~$78 bound and blank-endpoint ambiguity, and the assigned Working-date conventions.\n\n## Check results\n\n- **Passed:** coverage and materiality; participation continuity; dates and order (programmatic: non-decreasing Working dates, in-bounds, valid basis/method pairs); structure and consistency; evidence (every quotation recovered exactly from its cited passage).\n- **Qualified:** counts/population (6-vs-5 conflict, residual base assumption); offers/classifications (Insufficient-evidence levels); workbook operation.\n- **Not run / unsupported:** formulas were **not** recalculated in a spreadsheet application (LibreOffice headless crashed in this environment, even on a trivial file) — SUMIFS results (15 NDA; 28 contacts; R1 6; R2 3; residual 9) were verified by simulating the aggregation against the ledger. Internal links and the AI-original red-bold baseline highlighting were not rendered/tested in Excel; links are static and may need refreshing after sorting. No hidden/merged-cell tricks otherwise: the workbook is fully editable and correction-ready.","time":{"start":1789825291880,"end":1789825298886}}}
